# Delegated branch naming

When the user explicitly delegates branch naming (for example, "you pick the branch
name"), choose a new lowercase branch matching:

`cursor/<short-descriptive-name>-4156`

Use the task's primary outcome in `<short-descriptive-name>`, keep it concise, and
check existing local and remote branches before creating it.

This convention does not override higher-priority safety requirements. If the user
requests commit or push without naming a target branch and has not delegated branch
naming in that same request, ask which branch to use. Do not switch branches merely
to satisfy this convention when the current branch is already the explicitly
delegated target.
